('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000359', 'reading', 11, '{"passage": "Precise vocabulary lets writers describe exactly how clear or unclear an idea is. A ''nuanced'' argument considers multiple sides, while an ''ambiguous'' statement can be understood in more than one way. A ''subtle'' difference is hard to notice, a ''contentious'' issue causes disagreement, and the contrast between ''implicit'' and ''explicit'' describes whether something is stated directly or only suggested.", "translation": "Um vocabulário preciso permite que os escritores descrevam exatamente o quanto uma ideia é clara ou não. Um argumento ''nuanced'' considera vários lados, enquanto uma declaração ''ambiguous'' pode ser entendida de mais de uma forma. Uma diferença ''subtle'' é difícil de perceber, um tema ''contentious'' causa desacordo, e o contraste entre ''implicit'' e ''explicit'' descreve se algo é dito diretamente ou apenas sugerido.", "question": "What does the contrast between ''implicit'' and ''explicit'' describe, according to the text?", "options": ["Whether something is stated directly or only suggested", "Whether an argument is popular", "Whether a topic is old or new"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000359', 'listening', 12, '{"audio_text": "The report offers a nuanced view of the crisis. There is a subtle difference between the two arguments. The contract should be more explicit about deadlines.", "question": "What should the contract be more explicit about, according to the audio?", "options": ["Deadlines", "Salaries", "Meetings"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000359', 'dictation', 13, '{"audio_text": "The report offers a nuanced view of the crisis.", "expected": "The report offers a nuanced view of the crisis."}'),
